WEBVTT

00:00:06.883 --> 00:00:09.355
At Pentecost, Acts names Parthians,

00:00:09.355 --> 00:00:11.960
Medes and Elamites among the hearers.

00:00:12.073 --> 00:00:16.545
Later tradition calls them the first seed of the church in Persia;

00:00:16.545 --> 00:00:19.826
Acts itself says nothing of what they did next.

00:00:20.109 --> 00:00:22.997
The earliest datable evidence is Sasanian:

00:00:22.997 --> 00:00:25.247
a stamp seal with a Latin cross,

00:00:25.247 --> 00:00:28.728
catalogued by the British Museum as Early Sasanian.

00:00:29.011 --> 00:00:34.920
In the late third century the priest Kartir listed Christians among those he struck down.

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:37.606
Historians doubt a large persecution.

00:00:41.489 --> 00:00:44.099
About 340, Simeon bar Sabbae,

00:00:44.099 --> 00:00:49.649
head of the church, refused a double tax that Shapur II imposed for war with Rome,

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:50.998
and was executed.

00:00:51.281 --> 00:00:54.936
Sozomen counted over sixteen thousand martyrs by name.

00:00:55.049 --> 00:00:57.068
No independent count exists.

00:00:57.485 --> 00:01:04.929
In 410 about forty bishops met at Seleucia-Ctesiphon and made its bishop catholicos of the Persian church.

00:01:05.213 --> 00:01:09.749
By the seventh century the church had dioceses on the Persian Gulf.

00:01:10.063 --> 00:01:14.883
From Seleucia-Ctesiphon the church’s reach grew east across Central Asia.

00:01:14.997 --> 00:01:17.871
A priest of Balkh is named on the stele.

00:01:17.985 --> 00:01:20.769
A temple at Qocho left a wall painting.

00:01:20.883 --> 00:01:23.831
By 635 the road ended at Chang’an.

00:01:26.091 --> 00:01:29.625
The Xi’an Stele says it was erected in 781.

00:01:29.739 --> 00:01:36.139
It tells how a man named Alopen reached Chang’an in 635 and was received by the emperor.

00:01:36.423 --> 00:01:38.873
Chinese texts of the church survive,

00:01:38.873 --> 00:01:41.825
though some question the Osaka manuscripts.

00:01:41.939 --> 00:01:46.549
In 845 Emperor Wuzong’s edict devastated the church in China.

00:01:46.833 --> 00:01:50.953
The Arab conquest, between about 633 and 651,

00:01:50.953 --> 00:01:52.475
ended Sasanian rule.

00:01:52.589 --> 00:01:55.885
Christians lived on, protected but subordinate.

00:01:56.169 --> 00:02:00.911
In 1258 Doquz Khatun, a Christian wife of the Mongol Hulagu,

00:02:00.911 --> 00:02:03.837
is said to have interceded for Christians.

00:02:03.951 --> 00:02:05.505
The report is later.

00:02:05.789 --> 00:02:08.783
In 1287 the monk Rabban Bar Sauma,

00:02:08.783 --> 00:02:13.683
born in China, travelled as envoy of the Ilkhan Arghun to Constantinople,

00:02:13.683 --> 00:02:14.915
Rome and Paris.

00:02:15.199 --> 00:02:18.537
A letter of 1289, in Mongolian script,

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:20.297
names him as the envoy.

00:02:20.611 --> 00:02:25.339
In the early 1600s Shah Abbas I settled Armenians at New Julfa,

00:02:25.339 --> 00:02:27.505
across the river from Isfahan.

00:02:27.619 --> 00:02:29.923
How many, and how far by force,

00:02:29.923 --> 00:02:30.891
is debated.

00:02:31.175 --> 00:02:33.985
Vank Cathedral, begun in 1606,

00:02:33.985 --> 00:02:35.771
is covered in paintings.

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:39.474
At Urmia, on 21 November 1840,

00:02:39.474 --> 00:02:42.774
the American mission press was first set to work,

00:02:42.774 --> 00:02:46.699
with a few copies of the Lord’s Prayer in ancient Syriac.

00:02:46.982 --> 00:02:51.476
Around 1900, Christians, mostly Assyrians and Armenians,

00:02:51.476 --> 00:02:54.467
made up more than forty per cent of Urmia.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:59.381
The Constitutional Revolution produced a parliament in 1906.

00:02:59.494 --> 00:03:04.414
A law of 1909 gave four seats to recognised religious minorities,

00:03:04.414 --> 00:03:06.349
two of them to Christians.

00:03:08.132 --> 00:03:14.450
In 1915 nearly eighteen thousand Christians sheltered in the mission compounds at Urmia,

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:16.765
and disease killed many of them.

00:03:17.048 --> 00:03:20.001
Today Christians are a recognised minority.

00:03:20.114 --> 00:03:27.546
Estimates of their number run from about 118,000 in the 2011 census to several hundred thousand,

00:03:27.546 --> 00:03:31.169
because the census counts only recognised communities.
